Subject: code pointers in kernel text or the image; majors from the registry

From the stage-3 audit (amix-dlm docs/plan/stage-3-audit-2026-10-26.md
section 1.2, 1.4).  Plan patch 13: a switch entry or a qinit routine was
accepted anywhere in [stext, end), which includes kernel data and the
arena where other modules live.  dlm_okcode accepts 0, kernel text
[stext, etext) or the module's own image; a qinit's module_info and
module_stat must be in the image.  The registry now decides every
character major: dlm_creg, dlm_sreg and the driver linkage's drv_cmajor
refuse (ECONFIG) a major not registered to the module, and a row held by
another is ECONFIG, as C3-1 section 4 says (was EEXIST).  The harness's
registry names its drivers (pdm moves to its own major, 67); three
new checks.

